# Git commits

When the user asks to commit:

- Subject line only. No body, no bullet list, no "why" paragraph.
- One short line, under ~72 characters.
- Conventional prefix when it fits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `refactor:`.
- Describe what changed, not the story of the session.

```
# BAD — too long, nobody reads this
feat: add LLM-assisted experiment drafting with Gemini, fail-open
ExperimentLookup cache, generic demo routes, and dashboard delete
for AI-drafted experiments

This commit introduces several features to satisfy the assignment...

# GOOD
feat: add AI experiment drafting and fail-open assignment cache
```
